---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
---
<ContentLayout title="About StackGeist" description="How StackGeist approaches setup inspiration, gear recommendations, and affiliate links.">
  <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">StackGeist</a> / About</p>
  <p class="page-kicker">About StackGeist</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Useful setup ideas first. Affiliate links second.</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">StackGeist is a visual discovery project for gaming setups, desk setups, practical upgrades, and gear that solves a specific problem.</p>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><h2>How recommendations work</h2><p>We start with the setup problem, then look for products that fit the space, use case, and constraints. We do not invent testing, ratings, or personal ownership.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2>Affiliate disclosure</h2><p>Some retailer links are affiliate links. As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases. A commission does not change the price you pay.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2>What we verify</h2><p>Before publishing a product, we check the exact model and the specifications that matter to the recommendation. Price and stock can change after publication.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2>What we avoid</h2><p>No fake urgency, fake reviews, fabricated experience, or lists of products added only because they have an affiliate link.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>
